      "pClass": "productdescription",
      "pText": "The Tornado Climber is a long rope net course that children work through from start to finish. The net rises in waves, passes through tunnels and ends with a slide, so one run mixes climbing, crawling and sliding. It is a large piece, with a footprint of 54' x 18'10\" and a safe play area of 59' x 23'10\". That length suits a park edge, a resort lawn or a school ground where children can move in a line instead of crowding one spot. The frame is Horizon Teal with dark netting. Our 3-year warranty applies to the galvanised pipe frame, play rope and moulded parts. Send us your site measurements and we will show how the course runs across your ground."
